From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 16:11:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 16/17] port 7f86f97c: generate: STRATA_MSG_CKPT_TAIL=N
 checkpoints a prompt before its last message (opt-in, layer split too)

Adaptations to v0.2.12:
- The message-boundary site moved (read_part's cuts, ~19500) and the checkpoint save there now survives a failed
  copy (#3350); message_cut() replaces upstream's message_at expression and only the as_tail argument of that
  checkpoint_at changed, upstream's survivable-failure branch is kept as is.
- Beside --prompt-cache-tail: our cut is an ordinary checkpoint (as_tail false), so the one evict-first tail stays
  upstream's (--prompt-cache-tail's near-end chunk boundary, or STRATA_CACHE_MESSAGE_BOUNDARY's when MSG_CKPT_TAIL is
  unset); tail_ckpt_len is never set by it. When the batched read's tail checkpoint lands on the same length,
  checkpoint_at's existing rule turns it into a normal item (as for the turn checkpoint).
- The startup line sits after the STRATA_PARK_CAPTURE setup (the old STRATA_PARK_ASYNC anchor), the env helper after
  giveback_checks_env, message_cut_test after slot_chain_test in CMakeLists.
- Not in this commit: tools/msg_ckpt_check.py and the tools/vision_check_fake_engine.py hunk (they import
  vision_batch_check / cache_reuse_check and extend the fake engine of f8a41fff, on g3-212-vision only); they go on
  top of the integration branch.

STRATA_MSG_CKPT_TAIL unset: message_cut() returns upstream's expression (legacy && !multi_gpu, the tail kind), so
message_at and the as_tail flag are upstream's exactly.

(cherry picked from commit 7f86f97c100d619da8fdd0bda9157a7ce0554eee)

